    "stdout_tail": "        {\n                      \"quote_text\": \"## 4. Experiments\\n\\nFirst we compare YOLO with other real-time detection systems on PASCAL VOC 2007. To understand the differences between YOLO and R-CNN variants we explore the errors on VOC 2007 made by YOLO and Fast R-CNN, one of the highest performing versions of R-CNN [14]. Based on the different error profiles we show that YOLO can be used to rescore Fast R-CNN detections and reduce the errors from background false positives, giving a significant performance boost. We also present VOC 2012 results and compare mAP to current state-of-the-art methods. Finally, we show that YOLO generalizes to new domains better than other detectors on two artwork datasets.\\n\\n### 4.1. Comparison to Other Real-Time Systems\\n\\nMany research efforts in object detection focus on making standard detection pipeli\",\n                      \"work_id\": \"da37b10b-f5e6-4b74-9659-cc66e4abec26\",\n                      \"chunk_id\": \"e5ae8d20e9182ff1cd4a7ded8eb6166a71f8e8994b7650e7d2c0b900156e9a73\",\n                      \"chunk_fingerprint\": \"e5ae8d20e9182ff1cd4a7ded8eb6166a71f8e8994b7650e7d2c0b900156e9a73\",\n                      \"section\": \"You Only Look Once: Unified, Real-Time Object Detection / 4. Experiments\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"row_count\": 2,\n                  \"truncated\": false\n                }\n              ],\n              \"evidence_origin\": \"parent_tool\",\n              \"confidence\": 0.9,\n              \"terminal_state\": \"succeeded\",\n              \"failure_code\": null\n            }\n          ],\n          \"merge\": {\n            \"evidence_origin\": \"parent_tool\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.9,\n            \"conflict\": null,\n            \"writer_directive\": \"Evidence merge (v3): synthesize a single grounded answer. evidence_origin='parent_tool'. Do not hide tool denials, timeouts, or conflicting VERDICT lines; 